From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:08:12 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 74/76] flashnext cuda: a decode pass's BF16 hyper-connection
 read-out in two launches instead of five behind TF_FLASHNEXT_READOUT_DECODE

fn_hcn_down_act normalizes the streams in shared memory, runs the down on the qmmf lane's half-tile mma chains with its K slices summed in a cluster in slice order, then applies hc_reduce_act (act, its sums and the inject gates); fn_hcn_up1 is the prompt up+mix body at a 16-row tile. Same bits as fn_hc_normalize_cols, the lane's down, fn_hc_reduce_act, the lane's up and fn_hc_dense_mix8, checked by the read-out kernel contract at 1 to 63 rows. Passes of fewer than 64 rows only (verify windows and the draft head); default off.
